(This is a rework of my previous blueprint https://www.factorio.school/view/-NQZdJxlrO78t2sPVyI2, errors and unnecessary combinators have been removed, and the mechanics of the new version of the game have been used)

Shows the percentage of load on the electrical network. Suitable for nuclear power plants. Solar panels and batteries are not included!

How to use:
1. Find a free place where it will be convenient to see the indicator;
2. Build the "Wattmeter (part 2)" blueprint in this place;
3. Build the "Wattmeter (part 1)" blueprint near to the indicator;
4. Supply the reactor from the "Wattmeter (part 1)" with water and fuel, then start it manually by putting ONE fuel inside the reactor;
5. Wait until the first tank is filled with steam;
6. Disable or delete the combinator in which it is written to do this;
7. Wait until the second tank is filled with steam;
8. Connect the substation from the drawing "Wattmeter (part 1)" to any side substation from the drawing "Wattmeter (part 2)" with GREEN wire.

Enjoy!

(You can support the author here: https://boosty.to/dimuch62)

